hysical and artistic skills. Throughout the semester students will engage in a physical practice while learning creative tools for generating dance material, directing performance, and crafting choreographic ideas."},{"crn":"72290","code":"PCC","type":"Laboratory","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Laboratory","days":["M","W"],"start":780,"end":870,"location":"111 Dance Studio","instructors":["Caldarella, P"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"Using project-based learning, students will work in depth within each professor's choreographic process to hone their physical and artistic skills. Throughout the semester students will engage in a physical practice while learning creative tools for generating dance material, directing performance, and crafting choreographic ideas."}]},{"id":"DANC 260","title":"Dancing Techniques II","creditHours":"1 TO 5 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"63390","code":"A","type":"Laboratory","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Laboratory","days":["M","T","W","R"],"start":540,"end":630,"location":"103 Dance Studio","instructors":["Aprahamian, S","Hook, S","Oliver, C"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"This section meets FOUR days a week + mandatory FORUM attendance. Block I: Cynthia Oliver Block 2: Rebecca Medina Block 3: Serouj Aprahamian"},{"crn":"67619","code":"B","type":"Laboratory","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Laboratory","days":["M","T","W","R"],"start":540,"end":630,"location":"103 Dance Studio","instructors":["Aprahamian, S","Hook, S","Oliver, C"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"This section meets TWO days a week + mandatory FORUM attendance. Block I: Cynthia Oliver Block 2: Rebecca Medina Block 3: Serouj Aprahamian"}]},{"id":"DANC 270","title":"Dancing in Community I & II","creditHours":"1 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"74256","code":"A","type":"Laboratory","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Laboratory","days":["F"],"start":540,"end":630,"location":"2500 Krannert Center for Perf Arts","instructors":["Hanson, S"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"Dancing in Community II is a mixed level course which allows dance majors to dance together once a week and ACTIVATE the various perspectives and skills of a multi-level community. Students enrolled in DANC 160 and 260 should also enroll in DANC 270. This course is an exploration of varied movement practices that build community and ensemble approaches to dancing. To provide a balance of training from a range of cultural origins and traditions, this course will DELVE into 2-3 contemporary movement approaches per semester."}]},{"id":"DANC 301","title":"Yoga Fundamentals","creditHours":"1 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"61856","code":"A","type":"Laboratory","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Laboratory","days":["M","W"],"start":480,"end":530,"location":"2500 Krannert Center for Perf Arts","instructors":["Marini, N"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"Introduces basic yoga asana (postures) and an overview of the 8-limb system of yoga. Focus will be on physical understanding, correct alignment and inner awareness in the major basic poses. Weekly home practice, ongoing journal, and creation of a personal self-practice are required. Course Information: May be repeated in separate terms to a maximum of 16 hours. For students not enrolled in Yoga Teacher Training."}]},{"id":"DANC 316","title":"Dancing Techniques Elective","creditHours":"1 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"74286","code":"B","type":"Laboratory","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Laboratory","days":["T","R"],"start":780,"end":860,"location":"2500 Krannert Center for Perf Arts","instructors":["Henss, J"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":""},{"crn":"74288","code":"C","type":"Laboratory","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Laboratory","days":["M","W"],"start":540,"end":620,"location":"2127 Krannert Center for Perf Arts","instructors":["Wahrendorf, C"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":""},{"crn":"74656","code":"E","type":"Laboratory","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Laboratory","days":["T","R"],"start":1020,"end":1100,"location":"Su